  "context_needed": "BRAC's CFPR (Targeting the Ultra Poor) phase I, Bangladesh. Treated = ultra-poor households selected into the programme; controls = households identified as poor in the community wealth ranking but not selected (p. 13). Panel rounds 2002 (baseline), 2005, 2008 and 2011. Estimator: regression of the change in the outcome on treatment, weighted by inverse propensity scores; estimand ATT (pp. 16-17). The text on p. 17 explains the columns: 2005, 2008 and 2011 are each compared with 2002 to give short-, medium- and long-term effects (D1-D3), 'and thereafter we compare 2008 with 2005 and 2011 with 2008 to quantify the incremental effects' (D4, D5). So D4 and D5 are changes in the effect between rounds, not effects since baseline; the numbers agree (cowbull_a: D1 1.466 + D4 -0.529 = 0.937, against D2 0.936). Variable definitions are in Table 1 (p. 42): counts of animals or trees, and 0/1 indicators for savings and loans.",
